214	<h2>Words used on this page</h2>
215	<dl class="gloss">
216	<dt>coordinator</dt><dd>Coordinating session.</dd>
217	<dt>batch</dt><dd>Run of the batch workflow that takes several rungs at once, merges them and lands them together.</dd>
218	<dt>batch record</dt><dd>File that the planner writes before a batch&rsquo;s launch, whose rung sections are the workers&rsquo; briefs and whose other sections are for you.</dd>
219	<dt>PLAN</dt><dd>File of the record that holds the phases of the work, the questions for you in order, and the review lists.</dd>
220	<dt>PLAN&rsquo;s road</dt><dd>Work that the phases of PLAN list, in their order.</dd>
221	<dt>go</dt><dd>Your word that lets a batch or a new deliverable start.</dd>
222	<dt>rung</dt><dd>One piece of work in a batch, done by its own worker in its own worktree.</dd>
223	<dt>gather</dt><dd>Stage of a batch that merges the rungs, and folds their reports and record lines into the main tree.</dd>
224	<dt>manifest</dt><dd>Batch&rsquo;s list of its rungs, which the batch workflow reads.</dd>
225	<dt><code>landsOnlyWith</code></dt><dd>Field of the manifest that ties a rung to another, so that it lands only if the other lands too.</dd>
226	<dt>climb batch</dt><dd>Batch of PLAN&rsquo;s phases, numbered in order.</dd>
227	<dt><code>asif</code></dt><dd>Type assumption, written <code>e asif T</code>, which has a call treat the value of <code>e</code> as of its supertype <code>T</code>, to reach a supertrait&rsquo;s method; the code generator cannot compile it yet.</dd>
228	<dt>trait table</dt><dd>Code generator&rsquo;s table of an object&rsquo;s traits, which misses a trait in some objects that extend a trait of an imported api, and the name of the rung that fixes it.</dd>
229	<dt>main tree</dt><dd>Checkout of the repository at <code>/home/user/fortress</code>, not a worktree, where the gather and the stages after it work.</dd>
230	<dt>worktree</dt><dd>Second checkout of the repository in a folder of its own, where one agent works apart from the others.</dd>
231	<dt>skeptic</dt><dd>Agent that checks a rung&rsquo;s result after its worker, and fixes what it finds, test first.</dd>
232	<dt>point to report</dt><dd>Change of a kind that you review after the landing, which a rung lists with its evidence.</dd>
233	<dt>held push</dt><dd>Push of a batch that the batch workflow holds back, which leaves the batch&rsquo;s commits on the local <code>main</code> only.</dd>
234	<dt><code>pushHeld</code>, <code>heldBy</code></dt><dd>Fields of the batch workflow&rsquo;s result: whether it held the push, and the points that held it.</dd>
235	<dt>post-batch review</dt><dd>Check of a landed batch by one Opus reviewer, step 3 of the landing.</dd>
236	<dt>standing go</dt><dd>Go given once, in a skill, which holds for every case that it names.</dd>
237	<dt>hold</dt><dd>Decision that the work waits on until you answer.</dd>
238	<dt>judge, in a batch</dt><dd>Agent that rules on a fix that a skeptic contests, on a rung that the skeptic refuses, or on a rung whose worker could not go on.</dd>
239	<dt>skill writer</dt><dd>Headless session that makes every edit of the project skills.</dd>
240	<dt>compaction</dt><dd>Summary of the coordinator&rsquo;s conversation that replaces it when its context fills.</dd>
241	<dt>light boot</dt><dd>Boot at your word that skips the reading of FACTS, POSITIONS and INDEX, and searches them instead.</dd>
242	<dt>full boot</dt><dd>Boot of all its steps, 0 to 8, which reads FACTS, POSITIONS and INDEX; the default.</dd>
243	<dt>FACTS</dt><dd>File of the record that holds what the project has established, <code>FACTS.md</code>.</dd>
244	<dt>POSITIONS</dt><dd>File of the record that holds the project&rsquo;s decisions, <code>POSITIONS.md</code>.</dd>
245	<dt>INDEX</dt><dd>File of the record that lists its entries by subject.</dd>
246	<dt>batch landing</dt><dd>End of a batch, when its commit stage ends and the chain of steps that brings the record in line starts.</dd>
247	<dt>context</dt><dd>Coordinator&rsquo;s working memory between two compactions.</dd>
248	<dt><code>facts-extract.sh</code></dt><dd>Script that searches the record and prints the matching entries.</dd>
249	<dt>permission check</dt><dd>Check of the session that allows or refuses each command before it runs.</dd>
250	<dt>cloud container</dt><dd>Virtual machine with its own disk, on which a cloud session of Claude Code runs, such as the coordinator&rsquo;s.</dd>
251	<dt><code>cloud-container</code></dt><dd>Skill that holds how the cloud platform behaves, for every agent that works in a cloud container.</dd>
252	<dt>scratch branch</dt><dd>Branch made only for a test, with no work on it to keep.</dd>
253	<dt>record</dt><dd>Project&rsquo;s memory: the files under <code>explorations/</code> that hold what the project has established, decided and measured.</dd>
254	<dt>tree</dt><dd>Repository&rsquo;s files and git history as they stand.</dd>
255	<dt>ask</dt><dd>Decision that the coordinator puts to you in chat, with its options and a recommendation.</dd>
256	<dt>close</dt><dd>Proposed end of an open item, such as one on the closing docket.</dd>
257	<dt>held list</dt><dd>List of the points that you raise while you read turn by turn, and of the rules that you state, kept until the coordinator acts on them or they enter a skill.</dd>
258	<dt>review list</dt><dd>List in the plan of the decisions already taken that wait for your review.</dd>
259	<dt>docket</dt><dd>List of open items, each with a proposed close.</dd>
260	<dt>read mark</dt><dd>Your word that you read the page up to an item, such as a plain &ldquo;LGTM&rdquo; on a landed item, which drops that item and every older one at the next update.</dd>
261	<dt>boot note</dt><dd>File of what is in flight now, which the coordinator reads at each boot, with the links of the pages.</dd>
262	<dt>draft</dt><dd>Item under “Proposed changes” that waits for your yes.</dd>
263	<dt>page stage</dt><dd>Stage of the record-landing workflow that updates the page of <code>fortress-repo</code> changes.</dd>
264	<dt>diff</dt><dd>Text that shows what a change cut and added.</dd>
265	<dt>cold read</dt><dd>Reading of a changed part by a worker given only the skill, which marks each passage that would send it wrong or make it search.</dd>
266	<dt>authorship map</dt><dd>Map of who wrote what in the team's texts, compiled from the git history, in <code>research/authorship.md</code>.</dd>
267	<dt>cold reader</dt><dd>Worker that does a cold read.</dd>
268	<dt>flag</dt><dd>Passage that a cold read marks, with its problem and a proposed fix.</dd>
269	<dt>lint</dt><dd>Script that searches the skills' text for internal handles, status words and stale wording.</dd>
270	<dt>register</dt><dd>Way in which the coordinator writes to you, which the bullets at the head of “Talking to the curator” set.</dd>
271	<dt><code>fortress-repo</code></dt><dd>Skill that holds the rules that bind the workers in the repository.</dd>
272	<dt>revival part</dt><dd>Part of <code>fortress-repo</code> that tells workers how revived Fortress differs from the original.</dd>
273	<dt>closing docket</dt><dd>List of 3 November of the open items of the post-mortems and the held list, each with a proposed close.</dd>
274	<dt>commit stage</dt><dd>Last stage of a batch, which commits the landed tree and pushes it.</dd>
275	<dt>workflow journal</dt><dd>Log of a Workflow run, with a line for each agent's start and result.</dd>
276	<dt><code>spend.py</code></dt><dd>Script that counts the tokens written in the transcripts that changed after a given time.</dd>
277	<dt>quiz</dt><dd>Small set of decisions that a fresh worker answers from new entries, to test that their meaning stayed.</dd>
278	<dt>pilot</dt><dd>First run on three or four entries, which you read before the rest run.</dd>
279	<dt>chunk</dt><dd>Group of items that one writer takes in a round: about ten entries or rows in a long writing pass, 20 to 32 entries in a consolidation.</dd>
280	<dt>Workflow run</dt><dd>One launch of a workflow script by the Workflow tool, with its own ID and its own agents.</dd>
281	<dt>writer stream</dt><dd>Line of writer sessions in one run, each resumed while its context is small and its prompt cache warm.</dd>
282	<dt>judge</dt><dd>Agent at the end of a round that rules apply or hold on each point that a chunk's checks raise.</dd>
283	<dt>long writing pass</dt><dd>Run of a workflow that rewrites many entries or rows of the record, chunk by chunk.</dd>
284	<dt>record-landing workflow</dt><dd>Workflow that brings the record in line with a batch's landing.</dd>
285	<dt>revival page</dt><dd>Page that tells where the revival stands, which the record-landing workflow updates after a landing.</dd>
286	<dt>mining workflow</dt><dd>Workflow that finds where each POSITIONS entry came from.</dd>
287	<dt>clarity workflow</dt><dd>Workflow that rewrites entries so that each reads on its own.</dd>
288	<dt>orientation workflow</dt><dd>Workflow that writes and updates the revival part.</dd>
289	</dl>
