<p class="eyebrow">Fortress revival &middot; coordinator skill &middot; skill drafts &middot; version 24 &middot; 7 November 2026</p>
<h1>Your held rules, version 24</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Version 24. Two landed changes that you have not read, and two drafts that wait for your yes. Item 30, a new rule: a batch record takes every well-defined piece of work that moves the project forward, unless it would put the merge at risk, as you said this morning. Item 31, a rule whose meaning changed: while a batch runs, the coordinator commits in the main tree as usual until the gather starts, and changes nothing there from the gather&rsquo;s start until the batch&rsquo;s push. Draft 32: before every task of the skill writer that has its own cold read, the coordinator reads the held list and adds every point that waits for the writer. Draft 33: a held push goes out once the post-batch review finds nothing against it, with no second ask, unless it is held for a step that cannot be undone or for a change that still acts against your word.</p>
