<section id="words" class="part">
<h2>Words used on this page</h2>
<dl class="gloss">
<dt>coordinator</dt><dd>Coordinating session.</dd>
<dt>batch</dt><dd>Run of the batch workflow that takes several rungs at once, merges them and lands them together.</dd>
<dt>batch record</dt><dd>File that the planner writes before a batch&rsquo;s launch, whose rung sections are the workers&rsquo; briefs and whose other sections are for you.</dd>
<dt>PLAN</dt><dd>File of the record that holds the phases of the work, the questions for you in order, and the review lists.</dd>
<dt>PLAN&rsquo;s road</dt><dd>Work that the phases of PLAN list, in their order.</dd>
<dt>go</dt><dd>Your word that lets a batch or a new deliverable start.</dd>
<dt>rung</dt><dd>One piece of work in a batch, done by its own worker in its own worktree.</dd>
<dt>gather</dt><dd>Stage of a batch that merges the rungs, and folds their reports and record lines into the main tree.</dd>
<dt>manifest</dt><dd>Batch&rsquo;s list of its rungs, which the batch workflow reads.</dd>
<dt><code>landsOnlyWith</code></dt><dd>Field of the manifest that ties a rung to another, so that it lands only if the other lands too.</dd>
<dt>climb batch</dt><dd>Batch of PLAN&rsquo;s phases, numbered in order.</dd>
<dt><code>asif</code></dt><dd>Type assumption, written <code>e asif T</code>, which has a call treat the value of <code>e</code> as of its supertype <code>T</code>, to reach a supertrait&rsquo;s method; the code generator cannot compile it yet.</dd>
<dt>trait table</dt><dd>Code generator&rsquo;s table of an object&rsquo;s traits, which misses a trait in some objects that extend a trait of an imported api, and the name of the rung that fixes it.</dd>
<dt>main tree</dt><dd>Checkout of the repository at <code>/home/user/fortress</code>, not a worktree, where the gather and the stages after it work.</dd>
<dt>worktree</dt><dd>Second checkout of the repository in a folder of its own, where one agent works apart from the others.</dd>
