<section id="words" class="part">
<h2>Words used on this page</h2>
<dl class="gloss">
<dt>coordinator</dt><dd>Coordinating session.</dd>
<dt>batch</dt><dd>Run of the batch workflow that takes several rungs at once, merges them and lands them together.</dd>
<dt>batch record</dt><dd>File that the planner writes before a batch&rsquo;s launch, whose rung sections are the workers&rsquo; briefs and whose other sections are for you.</dd>
<dt>PLAN</dt><dd>File of the record that holds the phases of the work, the questions for you in order, and the review lists.</dd>
<dt>PLAN&rsquo;s road</dt><dd>Work that the phases of PLAN list, in their order.</dd>
<dt>go</dt><dd>Your word that lets a batch or a new deliverable start.</dd>
<dt>rung</dt><dd>One piece of work in a batch, done by its own worker in its own worktree.</dd>
<dt>gather</dt><dd>Stage of a batch that merges the rungs, and folds their reports and record lines into the main tree.</dd>
<dt>manifest</dt><dd>Batch&rsquo;s list of its rungs, which the batch workflow reads.</dd>
<dt><code>landsOnlyWith</code></dt><dd>Field of the manifest that ties a rung to another, so that it lands only if the other lands too.</dd>
<dt>climb batch</dt><dd>Batch of PLAN&rsquo;s phases, numbered in order.</dd>
<dt><code>asif</code></dt><dd>Type assumption, written <code>e asif T</code>, which has a call treat the value of <code>e</code> as of its supertype <code>T</code>, to reach a supertrait&rsquo;s method; the code generator cannot compile it yet.</dd>
<dt>trait table</dt><dd>Code generator&rsquo;s table of an object&rsquo;s traits, which misses a trait in some objects that extend a trait of an imported api, and the name of the rung that fixes it.</dd>
<dt>main tree</dt><dd>Checkout of the repository at <code>/home/user/fortress</code>, not a worktree, where the gather and the stages after it work.</dd>
<dt>worktree</dt><dd>Second checkout of the repository in a folder of its own, where one agent works apart from the others.</dd>
<dt>skeptic</dt><dd>Agent that checks a rung&rsquo;s result after its worker, and fixes what it finds, test first.</dd>
<dt>point to report</dt><dd>Change of a kind that you review after the landing, which a rung lists with its evidence.</dd>
<dt>held push</dt><dd>Push of a batch that the batch workflow holds back, which leaves the batch&rsquo;s commits on the local <code>main</code> only.</dd>
<dt><code>pushHeld</code>, <code>heldBy</code></dt><dd>Fields of the batch workflow&rsquo;s result: whether it held the push, and the points that held it.</dd>
<dt>post-batch review</dt><dd>Check of a landed batch by one Opus reviewer, step 3 of the landing.</dd>
<dt>standing go</dt><dd>Go given once, in a skill, which holds for every case that it names.</dd>
<dt>hold</dt><dd>Decision that the work waits on until you answer.</dd>
<dt>judge, in a batch</dt><dd>Agent that rules on a fix that a skeptic contests, on a rung that the skeptic refuses, or on a rung whose worker could not go on.</dd>
<dt>skill writer</dt><dd>Headless session that makes every edit of the project skills.</dd>
<dt>compaction</dt><dd>Summary of the coordinator&rsquo;s conversation that replaces it when its context fills.</dd>
<dt>light boot</dt><dd>Boot at your word that skips the reading of FACTS, POSITIONS and INDEX, and searches them instead.</dd>
<dt>full boot</dt><dd>Boot of all its steps, 0 to 8, which reads FACTS, POSITIONS and INDEX; the default.</dd>
<dt>FACTS</dt><dd>File of the record that holds what the project has established, <code>FACTS.md</code>.</dd>
<dt>POSITIONS</dt><dd>File of the record that holds the project&rsquo;s decisions, <code>POSITIONS.md</code>.</dd>
<dt>INDEX</dt><dd>File of the record that lists its entries by subject.</dd>
<dt>batch landing</dt><dd>End of a batch, when its commit stage ends and the chain of steps that brings the record in line starts.</dd>
<dt>context</dt><dd>Coordinator&rsquo;s working memory between two compactions.</dd>
<dt><code>facts-extract.sh</code></dt><dd>Script that searches the record and prints the matching entries.</dd>
<dt>permission check</dt><dd>Check of the session that allows or refuses each command before it runs.</dd>
<dt>cloud container</dt><dd>Virtual machine with its own disk, on which a cloud session of Claude Code runs, such as the coordinator&rsquo;s.</dd>
<dt><code>cloud-container</code></dt><dd>Skill that holds how the cloud platform behaves, for every agent that works in a cloud container.</dd>
<dt>scratch branch</dt><dd>Branch made only for a test, with no work on it to keep.</dd>
<dt>record</dt><dd>Project&rsquo;s memory: the files under <code>explorations/</code> that hold what the project has established, decided and measured.</dd>
<dt>tree</dt><dd>Repository&rsquo;s files and git history as they stand.</dd>
<dt>ask</dt><dd>Decision that the coordinator puts to you in chat, with its options and a recommendation.</dd>
<dt>close</dt><dd>Proposed end of an open item, such as one on the closing docket.</dd>
<dt>held list</dt><dd>List of the points that you raise while you read turn by turn, and of the rules that you state, kept until the coordinator acts on them or they enter a skill.</dd>
<dt>review list</dt><dd>List in the plan of the decisions already taken that wait for your review.</dd>
<dt>docket</dt><dd>List of open items, each with a proposed close.</dd>
<dt>read mark</dt><dd>Your word that you read the page up to an item, such as a plain &ldquo;LGTM&rdquo; on a landed item, which drops that item and every older one at the next update.</dd>
<dt>boot note</dt><dd>File of what is in flight now, which the coordinator reads at each boot, with the links of the pages.</dd>
