<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, &ldquo;The record: what goes where&rdquo;, the bullet on committing, line 234, its last sentence</p>
<ul><li>Commit only the paths that you name. Commit a tracked file with <code>git commit -- &lt;paths&gt;</code>, which is the same as <code>git commit --only &lt;paths&gt;</code>. For a new file, first run <code>git add -- &lt;paths&gt;</code>, with the paths named, then commit it in the same way. Never use <code>git add -A</code>, <code>git add .</code> or <code>git commit -a</code>, and never commit without paths: each takes changes that are not yours. The main tree is the checkout at <code>/home/user/fortress</code>, not a worktree, and a batch&rsquo;s gather stages its files there. While a batch runs, <span class="cut">edit nothing tracked there (<code>references/batch.md</code>, &ldquo;While it runs&rdquo;).</span> <span class="add">change the main tree only as <code>references/batch.md</code>, &ldquo;While it runs&rdquo;, allows.</span></li></ul>
